        "original_id": "307ada2a-9e56-54cb-a8bb-bf3806353dd1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Erlend Øye, Stuart Lee Murdoch\n- Music groups: Kings of Convenience, Belle and Sebastian, The Whitest Boy Alive, Hjálmar\n- Places: Bergen, Norway, Glasgow, Reykjavík, Seoul, Iceland, Scotland\n- Products: Legao, \"Garota\"\n- Roles: lead singer, songwriter, musician, writer, filmmaker\n\nFacts:\n- Stuart Lee Murdoch was born on 25 August 1968.\n- Kings of Convenience is an indie folk-pop duo from Bergen, Norway.\n- Belle and Sebastian is a Scottish band that formed in Glasgow in January 1996.\n- Stuart Lee Murdoch is a Scottish musician, writer, and filmmaker, and he is the lead singer and songwriter for Belle and Sebastian.\n- Legao is the second solo album by Erlend Øye, who is a singer in Kings of Convenience and The Whitest Boy Alive.\n- Erlend Øye recorded Legao in Reykjavík with Hjálmar, a reggae group from Iceland.\n- The single \"Garota\" from Legao was promoted by a videoclip shot in Seoul.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
